+
+## Rate limiting
+
+Fixed-window limit per API key, set with `createServer({ rateLimit: { limit, windowMs } })`. Defaults to `{ limit: 60, windowMs: 60000 }`. Windows are timed with the `now` option.
+
+- The key is the `x-api-key` header. Requests without it share the key `anonymous`.
+- A key's window starts at its first request and lasts `windowMs`. The first `limit` requests in a window are allowed. The first request after the window ends starts a new one.
+- The limiter runs before routing and authentication, so 401, 403 and 404 responses count too.
+- Rejected requests get `429` with `Retry-After` (whole seconds until the window ends, rounded up, at least 1) and the body `{"error": "rate_limited", "retryAfter": <seconds>}`.
+- Every limited response carries `X-RateLimit-Limit` and `X-RateLimit-Remaining` (requests left in the window after this one, never below 0).
+- `GET /health` is exempt. It is never limited, never counted, and has no rate-limit headers.
